      "extract": "Quantum Geometry [@thiembook; @rovbook; @alrev] provides microscopic degrees of freedom that account for the black-hole entropy. The issue was raised in works by Krasnov [@krasentropy] and Rovelli [@roventropy]. The final quantum Isolated Horizon framework was introduced by Ashtekar, Baez, Corichi and Krasnov [@abk]. The framework describes a black-hole in equilibrium surrounded by a quite arbitrary space-time. In",
